  "limits": [
    "The creature policy ranks paired value prefixes, not every possible creature subset. Paid native outcomes use two fixed paired seeds and the existing shared deadline.",
    "The pile policy places all eligible permanents in its first pile. It is legal but not an optimal partition strategy; branch controls do not establish random distribution fairness.",
    "Seeded player-order correction changes replay association, not the probability assigned to any pile.",
    "Explicit manual rules controllers and setup control layers are distinguished from actual paid AI-admission witnesses.",
    "Shroud, phasing, protection and Assault Suit native rules controls passed before the patch; they are retained controls, not claimed preexisting engine bugs.",
    "The two API entries do not establish an unsupported-card count or full gameplay coverage."
  ],
